  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6005.01 Applicability of Local Ordinances",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6005.01 Applicability of Local Ordinances. The state fire marshal shall determine whether any local law or ordinances and their application and enforcement provide an equivalent or greater degree of safety than that provided under the provisions of the fire code, and if not, the state fire code shall apply.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Saf-C 6000) #13094, eff 8-25-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6000.html"
